course: dictionary
lesson: 14235
title: Strong words that make you feel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words do more than name a thing. They make you feel something too. Nauseating is one of these words: it describes something so unpleasant that it makes you feel sick in your stomach. «The bins behind the school had a nauseating smell in the summer heat.» You can almost feel the sick feeling yourself.
explain: Look at the words around it to be sure. The clues are bins, summer heat and smell. Hot bins give off a bad smell, so nauseating must mean something that makes you feel sick. Check by swapping in a simpler phrase, "a very bad smell", and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word can also mean something very annoying, with no sick feeling at all. «Her endless bragging about her new bike was nauseating.» Nobody is ill here. The bragging is simply very irritating. When a word has two meanings, the context tells you which one the author means.
explain: Nauseating is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a smell or a trip. Its verb is nauseate, and its comparison form is more nauseating. Notice that the spelling changes a little from nauseate to nauseating.
fact: Nauseating means making you feel sick, as if you might be sick.
fact: «Nauseating» can also mean very annoying or unpleasant, as in «nauseating showing-off».
fact: Nauseate is the verb: a bad smell can nauseate you, which means it makes you feel sick.
fact: It is often used about smells, sights and movement, as in «a nauseating boat trip», which is a rocking trip that makes you feel ill.
fact: Context clues show which meaning fits: a smell suggests a sick feeling, while bragging suggests annoyance.
exercise: «The bins behind the school gave off a nauseating smell.» What does nauseating mean here? | Very cheerful and bright | Brand new | Loud and noisy | *Making you feel sick
exercise: «Her endless bragging about her new bike was nauseating.» What does nauseating mean here? | Making you feel sick in your stomach | Very old | *Very annoying | Giving out light
exercise: Which of these words is a verb form of nauseating? | ancient | *nauseate | glum | happy
test: «The fumes from the paint were so nauseating that we opened every window.» What does nauseating mean? | *Making you feel sick | Quiet and calm | Very beautiful | Cheap and common
test: Jayden moans, «Your constant teasing is nauseating!» What does he mean? | *Your teasing is very annoying | Your teasing is pretty | Your teasing is quiet and soft | Your teasing makes him feel sick
exam: Which sentence uses nauseating to mean very annoying? | «The rocking boat made the whole class feel ill, and it was nauseating.» | «The fumes from the drain were nauseating and made my eyes water.» | «The rotten fish gave off a nauseating smell.» | *«His endless boasting about his trophies was nauseating.»
